    body: "Implement a fun, streamlined web game called \"Brexit Border Dash\" where players must carefully navigate goods across a digital border, avoiding customs pitfalls and maximizing their profits.\n\nFeatures:\n- Create a 2D game area representing a border crossing, with a clear dividing line in the middle. The left side is the 'EU Market' and the right side is the 'UK Market'.\n- Display a small, simple 'delivery truck' sprite that the player controls, starting on the EU side.\n- Implement smooth horizontal movement for the truck using the left and right arrow keys. Ensure that the default keystroke behavior is disabled.\n- Generate various 'goods' items (represented by simple icons like a box, a barrel, a crate) that appear randomly on the EU side and move towards the border.\n- Each good item should have a randomly assigned 'value' (displayed as a small number next to it) and a 'customs risk' (represented by a small, colored icon: green for low, yellow for medium, red for high).\n- Create 'customs checkpoints' as static obstacles on the border line. These checkpoints should have varying 'strictness' levels, visually indicated by their size or color intensity.\n- When a good item reaches a customs checkpoint, it should either pass through successfully (if its customs risk is lower than the checkpoint's strictness) or be 'detained' (if its risk is higher). Detained items disappear and result in a penalty.\n- Display a 'profit' counter at the top of the screen that increases when goods successfully cross the border (adding their value) and decreases when goods are detained.\n- Implement a 'caution meter' that fills up as the player takes risks (e.g., attempting to cross high-risk goods through strict checkpoints). If the caution meter fills completely, it's 'Game Over'.\n- Add a timer that counts down from 90 seconds. When the timer hits 0 seconds, display a \"Game Over\" screen that shows the final profit, and allows the user to restart the game.\n- The game should use a color scheme inspired by official EU and UK government branding, with blues, reds, and whites, but with a slightly muted, cautious tone.\n\nUser Actions:\n1. Use the left and right arrow keys to move your delivery truck horizontally along the EU side, positioning it to collect goods and guide them towards the border.\n2. Press the spacebar to activate 'Cautious Crossing' mode, which temporarily highlights the safest path through customs checkpoints for 3 seconds (can be used once every 20 seconds).\nNote:\n- Your output should be implemented in JavaScript with HTML and CSS.\n- Ensure that the output has both index.js and index.html files\n",
