    body: 'Implement a fun, streamlined web game called "Phrase Explorer" where players learn unique dialect phrases by matching them to their meanings in a vibrant, travel-themed setting.\n\nFeatures:\n- Create a visually appealing 2D game area with a background depicting a stylized world map or famous landmarks, using warm, inviting colors (e.g., terracotta, olive green, deep blue).\n- Display a central "Phrase Card" area where a unique dialect phrase appears prominently.\n- Below the Phrase Card, display three "Meaning Cards" arranged horizontally. Each Meaning Card should contain a potential meaning for the phrase, with only one being correct.\n- Implement a scoring system: +100 points for a correct match, -50 points for an incorrect match.\n- Add a timer that counts down from 60 seconds. When the timer hits 0, display a "Game Over" screen showing the final score and a "Play Again" button.\n- When a correct match is made, the Phrase Card and the correct Meaning Card should briefly glow with a golden animation, and a new set of phrase and meaning cards should appear.\n- When an incorrect match is made, the selected Meaning Card should briefly flash red, and the correct Meaning Card should briefly flash green, before a new set of cards appears.\n- Display the current score and the remaining time prominently at the top of the screen.\n- The phrases and meanings should be presented in a clear, easy-to-read font, resembling handwritten notes on old travel postcards.\n- Ensure a smooth transition between rounds, with new cards fading in.\n\nUser Actions:\n1. Click on one of the three Meaning Cards to select what you believe is the correct meaning for the displayed phrase.\n2. Press the \'Spacebar\' to skip the current phrase and get a new one, but this will incur a 20-point penalty.\nNote:\n- Your output should be implemented in JavaScript with HTML and CSS.\n- Ensure that the output has both index.js and index.html files\n',
