    body: "Implement an interactive simulation demonstrating the concept of a 'Bag of Words' model in Natural Language Processing (NLP), visualized as a data pipeline. The simulation should highlight how text is processed and transformed into a numerical representation for machine learning models.\n\nFeatures:\n- Create a visual representation of a data pipeline, with distinct stages: 'Input Text', 'Tokenization', 'Normalization', and 'Vectorization'. Each stage should be a clearly defined rectangular box or container.\n- The 'Input Text' stage should contain a text area where users can type or paste sentences.\n- The 'Tokenization' stage should display individual words (tokens) extracted from the input text, each as a separate, draggable element. Tokens should appear in the order they are found in the input.\n- The 'Normalization' stage should display the tokens after they have been converted to lowercase and had punctuation removed. Each normalized token should also be a separate, draggable element.\n- The 'Vectorization' stage should display a dynamic 'Bag of Words' vector. This vector should be a series of numerical values (e.g., counts) corresponding to a predefined vocabulary. The vocabulary should be dynamically built from all unique words processed through the pipeline.\n- Visual cues should indicate the flow of data: when text is processed, tokens should visually move from 'Input Text' to 'Tokenization', then to 'Normalization', and finally contribute to the 'Vectorization' stage.\n- The background should have a dark, tech-inspired theme (e.g., dark blue/grey with subtle circuit board patterns) and the pipeline stages should have clean, modern borders (e.g., light blue or green glowing lines).\n- Display a 'Vocabulary' list alongside the vectorization stage, showing the unique words and their corresponding index in the vector.\n- Implement a 'Reset' button styled as a server reboot icon.\n\nUser Actions:\n1. Type or paste text into the 'Input Text' area. Pressing 'Enter' or clicking an 'Process' button (which appears when text is entered) should trigger the pipeline to process the text, with tokens flowing through each stage and updating the vector.\n2. Click and drag individual tokens from the 'Tokenization' or 'Normalization' stages to reorder them or temporarily remove them from the pipeline. Removing a token should update the 'Vectorization' stage accordingly.\nNote:\n- Your output should be implemented in JavaScript with HTML and CSS.\n- Ensure that the output has both index.js and index.html files\n",
