    body: "Create an interactive simulation of a card dealing process that visualizes the principles of statistical distribution and randomness, inspired by a casino supervisor's perspective.\n\nFeatures:\n- Create a top-down view of a rectangular card table with a green felt surface and a subtle wooden border. The table should occupy most of the screen.\n- Display a deck of cards (represented by a single stack of cards) on one side of the table. The deck should visually decrease in size as cards are dealt.\n- Implement a dealing mechanism that distributes cards into multiple hands (e.g., 4 hands for 4 players) around the table. Each hand should be represented by a distinct area on the table.\n- As cards are dealt, they should visually animate from the deck to their respective hands. Each card should be represented by a simple rectangle, with its suit and rank (e.g., 'A♠', 'K♥') displayed.\n- Implement a real-time statistical display panel, styled like a digital casino display, showing:\n    * The number of cards remaining in the deck.\n    * The distribution of suits (Spades, Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs) dealt into each hand.\n    * The distribution of card ranks (A, K, Q, J, 10-2) dealt into each hand.\n- The display panel should update dynamically as cards are dealt.\n- Include visual effects for dealing, such as a subtle 'snap' sound effect (visualized as a quick flash) when a card lands in a hand.\n- The overall color scheme should be dark greens, rich browns, and gold accents, evoking a sophisticated casino atmosphere.\n- Create a 'Reset Table' button, styled like a polished casino chip, to clear all hands and reset the deck.\n\nUser Actions:\n1. Click the 'Deal Card' button (styled as a dealer's hand icon) to deal one card to each active hand in sequence. The dealing should pause briefly between each card to allow observation.\n2. Click the 'Shuffle Deck' button (styled as a deck of cards being shuffled) to randomly reorder the remaining cards in the deck. This action should not affect cards already dealt into hands.\nNote:\n- Your output should be implemented in JavaScript with HTML and CSS.\n- Ensure that the output has both index.js and index.html files\n",
